## Overview

- `variant` wins over `type`; with neither set, the button is `secondary`.
- `disabled`, `loading`, and an unfinished `progress` (`< 100` with no `status`) all disable the native `<button>` and suppress `click`; a loading `TxSplitButton` disables both sides.
- Non-block, non-circle buttons animate width with a FLIP transition when `loading`, `progress`, or `status` changes, and ease colour only inside the state-change window (`.is-morphing`); `block` with `circle` keeps the regular label layout.
- An icon-only `TxButton` takes its name from attrs such as `aria-label`; `TxIconButton` maps `label` to `aria-label` and a boolean `pressed` to `aria-pressed`.
- `TxCopyButton` uses the Clipboard API and falls back to `execCommand`; it ignores clicks while copying and eases colour only on a state change.
- Under reduced motion, the `vibrate` shake is skipped and both `TxButton` status and `TxCopyButton` land each state as its final frame.

